cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RAGRAF in academic or technical work, please cite it as below."

title: "RAGRAF: a graph-and-vector knowledge base of code for LLM agents"
abstract: >-
  RAGRAF indexes a repository into three SQLite stores inside the indexed project — a
  symbol/call graph, an FTS5 lexicon with vectors, and a revision and drift ledger — and
  answers an agent's questions through a fixed set of 38 operations (40 tools over MCP):
  where a symbol is defined, who calls it, what a change affects, what is in a database
  table and who writes it, which files are copies, and whether a write matches the schema.
  Every fact carries a path:line reference and its provenance (stated or derived); an
  immutable index plus an append-only drift ledger keeps facts from different moments
  distinguishable; and an optional code-property-graph layer (Java + Joern) unlocks
  slicing, degrading honestly when absent. Measured on a real PHP portal: 14 navigation
  tasks took 28 tool calls without the index and 14 with it, with 92% first-query target
  hit rate, 100% verifiability, and no full-file reads.

